  "summary": "Preinstall beacon exfiltrates installer identity to Interactsh OAST callback",
  "details": "The preinstall lifecycle script executes `whoami`, `hostname`, and fetches the machine's public IP from ifconfig.me, then transmits all three as query-string parameters via curl (with wget fallback) to the hardcoded host kwphewvexhjbtfduscqybx6q7c862eh0g.oast.fun — an Interactsh out-of-band callback subdomain used to receive exfiltrated data. This fires automatically on `npm install`. The README claims the package makes no network requests, directly contradicting the shipped code.",
